{"book":"Acts","chapter":10,"translation":"KJV","url":"/bible/acts/10","verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"There was a certain man in Cesarea called Cornelius, a centurion of the band called the Italian band,","words":[["There was",["G2258"]],["a certain",["G5100"]],["man",["G435"]],["in",["G1722"]],["Cesarea",["G2542"]],["called",["G3686"]],["Cornelius,",["G2883"]],["a centurion",["G1543"]],["of",["G1537"]],["the band",["G4686"]],["called",["G2564"]],["the Italian band,",[]]]},{"verse":2,"text":"A devout man, and one that feared God with all his house, which gave much alms to the people, and prayed to God alway.","words":[["A devout",["G2152"]],["man, and",["G2532"]],["one that feared",["G5399"]],["God",["G2316"]],["with",["G4862"]],["all",["G3956"]],["his",["G846"]],["house,",["G3624"]],["which",["G5037"]],["gave",["G4160"]],["much",["G4183"]],["alms",["G1654"]],["to the people,",["G2992"]],["and",["G2532"]],["prayed",["G1189"]],["to God",["G2316"]],["alway.",[]]]},{"verse":3,"text":"He saw in a vision evidently about the ninth hour of the day an angel of God coming in to him, and saying unto him, Cornelius.","words":[["He saw",["G1492"]],["in",["G1722"]],["a vision",["G3705"]],["evidently",["G5320"]],["about",["G5616"]],["the ninth",["G1766"]],["hour",["G5610"]],["of the day",["G2250"]],["an angel",["G32"]],["of God",["G2316"]],["coming in",["G1525"]],["to",["G4314"]],["him,",["G846"]],["and",["G2532"]],["saying",["G2036"]],["unto him,",["G846"]],["Cornelius.",[]]]},{"verse":4,"text":"And when he looked on him, he was afraid, and said, What is it, Lord? And he said unto him, Thy prayers and thine alms are come up for a memorial before God.","words":[["And",["G1161"]],["when he looked",["G816"]],["on him,",["G846"]],["he was",["G1096"]],["afraid,",["G1719"]],["and",["G2532"]],["said,",["G2036"]],["What",["G5101"]],["is it,",["G2076"]],["Lord?",["G2962"]],["And",["G1161"]],["he said",["G2036"]],["unto him,",["G846"]],["Thy",["G4675"]],["prayers",["G4335"]],["and",["G2532"]],["thine",["G4675"]],["alms",["G1654"]],["are come up",["G305"]],["for",["G1519"]],["a memorial",["G3422"]],["before",["G1799"]],["God.",[]]]},{"verse":5,"text":"And now send men to Joppa, and call for one Simon, whose surname is Peter:","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["now",["G3568"]],["send",["G3992"]],["men",["G435"]],["to",["G1519"]],["Joppa,",["G2445"]],["and",["G2532"]],["call for",["G3343"]],["one Simon,",["G4613"]],["whose",["G3739"]],["surname is",["G1941"]],["Peter:",[]]]},{"verse":6,"text":"He lodgeth with one Simon a tanner, whose house is by the sea side: he shall tell thee what thou oughtest to do.","words":[["He",["G3778"]],["lodgeth",["G3579"]],["with",["G3844"]],["one",["G5100"]],["Simon",["G4613"]],["a tanner,",["G1038"]],["whose",["G3739"]],["house",["G3614"]],["is",["G2076"]],["by",["G3844"]],["the sea side:",["G2281"]],["he",["G3778"]],["shall tell",["G2980"]],["thee",["G4671"]],["what",["G5101"]],["thou",["G4571"]],["oughtest",["G1163"]],["to do.",[]]]},{"verse":7,"text":"And when the angel which spake unto Cornelius was departed, he called two of his household servants, and a devout soldier of them that waited on him continually;","words":[["And",["G1161"]],["when",["G5613"]],["the angel",["G32"]],["which",["G3588"]],["spake",["G2980"]],["unto Cornelius",["G2883"]],["was departed,",["G565"]],["he called",["G5455"]],["two",["G1417"]],["of his",["G846"]],["household servants,",["G3610"]],["and",["G2532"]],["a devout",["G2152"]],["soldier",["G4757"]],["of them that waited on",["G4342"]],["him",["G846"]],["continually;",[]]]},{"verse":8,"text":"And when he had declared all these things unto them, he sent them to Joppa.","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["when he had declared",["G1834"]],["all these things",["G537"]],["unto them,",["G846"]],["he sent",["G649"]],["them",["G846"]],["to",["G1519"]],["Joppa.",[]]]},{"verse":9,"text":"On the morrow, as they went on their journey, and drew nigh unto the city, Peter went up upon the housetop to pray about the sixth hour:","words":[["On the morrow,",["G1887"]],["as they",["G1565"]],["went on their journey,",["G3596"]],["and",["G2532"]],["drew nigh",["G1448"]],["unto the city,",["G4172"]],["Peter",["G4074"]],["went up",["G305"]],["upon",["G1909"]],["the housetop",["G1430"]],["to pray",["G4336"]],["about",["G4012"]],["the sixth",["G1623"]],["hour:",[]]]},{"verse":10,"text":"And he became very hungry, and would have eaten: but while they made ready, he fell into a trance,","words":[["And",["G1161"]],["he became",["G1096"]],["very hungry,",["G4361"]],["and",["G2532"]],["would",["G2309"]],["have eaten:",["G1089"]],["but",["G1161"]],["while they",["G1565"]],["made ready,",["G3903"]],["he",["G846"]],["fell",["G1968"]],["into",["G1909"]],["a trance,",[]]]},{"verse":11,"text":"And saw heaven opened, and a certain vessel descending unto him, as it had been a great sheet knit at the four corners, and let down to the earth:","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["saw",["G2334"]],["heaven",["G3772"]],["opened,",["G455"]],["and",["G2532"]],["a certain",["G5100"]],["vessel",["G4632"]],["descending",["G2597"]],["unto",["G1909"]],["him,",["G846"]],["as",["G5613"]],["it had been a great",["G3173"]],["sheet",["G3607"]],["knit",["G1210"]],["at the four",["G5064"]],["corners,",["G746"]],["and",["G2532"]],["let down",["G2524"]],["to",["G1909"]],["the earth:",[]]]},{"verse":12,"text":"Wherein were all manner of fourfooted beasts of the earth, and wild beasts, and creeping things, and fowls of the air.","words":[["Wherein",["G1722","G3739"]],["were",["G5225"]],["all manner",["G3956"]],["of fourfooted beasts",["G5074"]],["of the earth,",["G1093"]],["and",["G2532"]],["wild beasts,",["G2342"]],["and",["G2532"]],["creeping things,",["G2062"]],["and",["G2532"]],["fowls",["G4071"]],["of the air.",[]]]},{"verse":13,"text":"And there came a voice to him, Rise, Peter; kill, and eat.","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["there came",["G1096"]],["a voice",["G5456"]],["to",["G4314"]],["him,",["G846"]],["Rise,",["G450"]],["Peter;",["G4074"]],["kill,",["G2380"]],["and",["G2532"]],["eat.",[]]]},{"verse":14,"text":"But Peter said, Not so, Lord; for I have never eaten any thing that is common or unclean.","words":[["But",["G1161"]],["Peter",["G4074"]],["said,",["G2036"]],["Not so,",["G3365"]],["Lord;",["G2962"]],["for",["G3754"]],["I have",["G5315"]],["never",["G3763"]],["eaten",["G5315"]],["any thing",["G3956"]],["that is common",["G2839"]],["or",["G2228"]],["unclean.",[]]]},{"verse":15,"text":"And the voice spake unto him again the second time, What God hath cleansed, that call not thou common.","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["the voice",["G5456"]],["spake unto",["G4314"]],["him",["G846"]],["again",["G3825","G1537"]],["the second time,",["G1208"]],["What",["G3739"]],["God",["G2316"]],["hath cleansed,",["G2511"]],["that call",["G2840"]],["not",["G3361"]],["thou",["G4771"]],["common.",[]]]},{"verse":16,"text":"This was done thrice: and the vessel was received up again into heaven.","words":[["This",["G5124"]],["was done",["G1096"]],["thrice:",["G1909","G5151"]],["and",["G2532"]],["the vessel",["G4632"]],["was received up",["G353"]],["again",["G3825"]],["into",["G1519"]],["heaven.",[]]]},{"verse":17,"text":"Now while Peter doubted in himself what this vision which he had seen should mean, behold, the men which were sent from Cornelius had made enquiry for Simon’s house, and stood before the gate,","words":[["Now",["G1161"]],["while",["G5613"]],["Peter",["G4074"]],["doubted",["G1280"]],["in",["G1722"]],["himself",["G1438"]],["what",["G5101"]],["this vision",["G3705"]],["which",["G3739"]],["he had seen",["G1492"]],["should mean,",["G302","G1498"]],["behold,",["G2400","G2532"]],["the men",["G435"]],["which",["G3588"]],["were sent",["G649"]],["from",["G575"]],["Cornelius",["G2883"]],["had made enquiry",["G1331"]],["for Simon’s house,",["G3614"]],["and stood",["G2186"]],["before",["G1909"]],["the gate,",[]]]},{"verse":18,"text":"And called, and asked whether Simon, which was surnamed Peter, were lodged